DESCRIPTION:
  CLI-flag-gated command injection. The server must be started with --exec-mode
  for the /exec endpoint to execute commands. A user-supplied URL query
  parameter is copied into a local stack buffer via snprintf() and then passed
  to system() with no sanitization.

CONFIG_GATE (C1 — simple):
  mechanism:  CLI flag (--exec-mode), stored in global int exec_mode
  check:      single boolean guard at top of callback_exec():
              `if (!exec_mode)`
  complexity: one condition, one global flag, no struct, no utility function

INPUT_FLOW (I2 — snprintf buffer then system()):
  entry:      HTTP GET /exec?cmd=<payload>
  path:       callback_exec() reads cmd from request->map_url
              snprintf(cmd_buf, sizeof(cmd_buf), "%s", cmd) copies into buffer
              cmd_buf is then passed to system()
  transforms: one snprintf copy into a 1024-byte stack buffer; no truncation
              of exploitable payloads in practice

SANITIZATION (S1 — none):
  none

SINK:        system(cmd_buf) in callback_exec() (server.c)

CHANGED FILES:
  server.c — additions after callback_default():
    1. exec_mode global:   `static int exec_mode = 0;` (C1)
    2. callback_exec():    C1 gate + snprintf copy + system() call (I2+S1)
    3. main():             --exec-mode flag parsing + endpoint registration

EXPLOIT:
  build:   bash build.sh
  start:   ./ulfius_server --port 18101 --exec-mode
  trigger: curl 'http://127.0.0.1:18101/exec?cmd=id>/tmp/poc_101_marker'
  verify:  cat /tmp/poc_101_marker
  expect:  uid=... line written by the server process

  gate bypass: omitting --exec-mode causes /exec to return 403.

NOTES:
  - system() output goes to the server's stdout/stderr, not the HTTP response.
    The response body contains only "Command dispatched".
    Use a write-to-file payload (id>/tmp/marker) to confirm blind execution.
  - The snprintf copy (I2) adds one indirection vs I1 but does not prevent
    injection: shell metacharacters pass through snprintf unchanged.
  - Payloads up to 1023 bytes fit in cmd_buf; longer payloads are truncated.
